1
00:00:03,450 --> 00:00:05,220
<i>In this world...</i>

2
00:00:05,660 --> 00:00:10,990
<i>Is the destiny of mankind controlled by some transcendental entity or law?</i>

3
00:00:11,860 --> 00:00:14,890
<i>Is it like the hand of God hovering above?</i>

4
00:00:15,930 --> 00:00:17,660
<i>At least it is true...</i>

5
00:00:18,170 --> 00:00:21,830
<i>...that man has no control, even over his own will.</i>

6
00:00:24,880 --> 00:00:28,750
I want to ask you to kill a man for me.

7
00:00:29,550 --> 00:00:30,750
Kill a man?

8
00:00:30,750 --> 00:00:31,170
Who?

9
00:00:31,820 --> 00:00:35,020
The man who is next in line
to the throne of Midland...

10
00:00:35,020 --> 00:00:36,450
...Count Julius.

11
00:00:58,410 --> 00:01:00,490
Feel no shame about shape

12
00:01:00,580 --> 00:01:02,410
Weather changes their phrase

13
00:01:02,540 --> 00:01:06,170
Even mother will show you another way

14
00:01:06,170 --> 00:01:08,540
So put your glasses on

15
00:01:08,630 --> 00:01:10,630
Nothing will be wrong

16
00:01:10,710 --> 00:01:12,840
There's no blame. There's no fame

17
00:01:12,840 --> 00:01:14,670
It's up to you

18
00:01:14,840 --> 00:01:18,300
The first words should be found

19
00:01:18,930 --> 00:01:21,930
Whatever holds you back

20
00:01:22,810 --> 00:01:23,310
I...

21
00:01:23,680 --> 00:01:24,430
...can...

22
00:01:24,520 --> 00:01:26,600
I can get it off

23
00:01:26,600 --> 00:01:27,600
Tell me what...

24
00:01:27,600 --> 00:01:28,600
Tell me what...

25
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:30,440
Tell me what you want

26
00:01:30,560 --> 00:01:31,520
I don't know why...

27
00:01:31,730 --> 00:01:32,530
Don't know why...

28
00:01:32,530 --> 00:01:34,530
Don't know why you're afraid

29
00:01:34,690 --> 00:01:35,690
Tell me what...

30
00:01:35,780 --> 00:01:36,650
Tell me what...

31
00:01:36,820 --> 00:01:38,320
Tell me what you'd say

32
00:01:38,570 --> 00:01:39,660
I don't know why...

33
00:01:39,780 --> 00:01:40,740
Don't know why...

34
00:01:40,830 --> 00:01:41,530
Too late...

35
00:01:41,620 --> 00:01:43,160
It's too late

36
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:52,090
Noble Man

37
00:02:24,490 --> 00:02:25,700
Julius...

38
00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:26,790
I'm in luck.

39
00:02:30,250 --> 00:02:31,630
Who is that kid?

40
00:02:40,840 --> 00:02:42,010
Stand up, Adonis!

41
00:02:42,010 --> 00:02:43,430
How shameful you are!

42
00:02:43,430 --> 00:02:45,510
Were you really born of royal blood?

43
00:02:46,970 --> 00:02:47,980
Now stand up!

44
00:02:47,980 --> 00:02:49,230
Do not rest!

45
00:02:49,230 --> 00:02:51,650
Your enemies never let you rest in battle!

46
00:02:51,900 --> 00:02:54,820
Your Highness,
kindly call it a day for now...

47
00:02:54,820 --> 00:02:56,190
Do not disturb us, Hassan!

48
00:02:57,150 --> 00:02:58,860
Adonis will someday become...

49
00:02:58,860 --> 00:03:02,030
...commander of the White Dragon
Knights, the land's strongest troop!

50
00:03:02,450 --> 00:03:03,820
And that is not all!

51
00:03:04,240 --> 00:03:09,330
It is even possible that he will marry
Lady Charlotte and rule all Midland!

52
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:11,120
Those who were born into royalty...

53
00:03:11,120 --> 00:03:14,210
...must carry heavier burdens
than those who were not.

54
00:03:14,540 --> 00:03:16,920
Such a burden is his destiny!

55
00:03:18,380 --> 00:03:19,420
Fight on!

56
00:03:19,420 --> 00:03:21,880
Let's see you try to take
at least one match from me!

57
00:03:37,150 --> 00:03:38,820
So much for today.

58
00:03:42,030 --> 00:03:45,320
Keep yourself warm and
be ready for tomorrow's training.

59
00:03:49,410 --> 00:03:50,580
Master Adonis...

60
00:03:50,910 --> 00:03:53,250
...you're quite injured.
I will treat your wounds.

61
00:03:54,250 --> 00:03:56,630
Your father is desperate.

62
00:03:56,630 --> 00:04:01,170
As your only parent, he's just trying
to raise you into a full-fledged knight.

63
00:04:01,720 --> 00:04:04,890
You should not think ill of your father.

64
00:04:36,630 --> 00:04:39,800
Sir Griffith, we have heard your story...

65
00:04:39,800 --> 00:04:42,720
You protected the princess's
life with your own body...

66
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:44,260
How courageous you are!

67
00:04:44,260 --> 00:04:47,590
Your words are too kind.
I am really no more than a coward.

68
00:04:47,590 --> 00:04:48,600
Sir Griffith.

69
00:04:50,260 --> 00:04:53,270
Oh, it's Lord Raban and Lord Owen.

70
00:04:53,270 --> 00:04:56,020
That was a terrible affair
that occurred during the hunt.

71
00:04:56,850 --> 00:05:01,480
Indeed. We nearly lost
a vital asset of Midland's army.

72
00:05:01,480 --> 00:05:03,030
My life is nothing.

73
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:06,070
It is only important that
Princess Charlotte is safe from harm.

74
00:05:18,080 --> 00:05:20,880
Oh, she has become even more charming.

75
00:05:21,920 --> 00:05:24,510
She must be in love with someone.

76
00:05:28,840 --> 00:05:31,140
Your Highness, please excuse my tongue.

77
00:05:31,140 --> 00:05:35,020
However, your rigorous lessons have
become even more demanding of late.

78
00:05:35,430 --> 00:05:37,640
I understand what you're going through...

79
00:05:37,640 --> 00:05:41,070
...but you should be a little
easier on the young master.

80
00:05:41,070 --> 00:05:42,610
I know.

81
00:05:42,900 --> 00:05:45,990
Lately, I have had little success
with my duties in the royal court.

82
00:05:46,700 --> 00:05:50,280
Due to such affairs,
I have become quite irritated.

83
00:05:51,030 --> 00:05:54,040
I earnestly beg you not
to overextend yourself.

84
00:06:30,610 --> 00:06:31,870
Is it the wind?

85
00:06:40,170 --> 00:06:41,040
What?

86
00:06:41,040 --> 00:06:41,880
A burglar?

87
00:07:04,310 --> 00:07:06,940
I-I know you...

88
00:07:07,610 --> 00:07:08,900
You are...

89
00:07:09,360 --> 00:07:10,360
...Griffith's...

90
00:07:22,290 --> 00:07:23,250
Excuse me...

91
00:07:25,590 --> 00:07:27,130
B-Burglar?

92
00:07:28,380 --> 00:07:29,170
He saw...

93
00:07:54,450 --> 00:07:55,620
H-Hey...

94
00:08:07,460 --> 00:08:09,300
What was that noise?

95
00:08:09,300 --> 00:08:10,670
What is happening, Your Highness?

96
00:08:12,010 --> 00:08:13,930
M-Master Adonis!

97
00:08:13,930 --> 00:08:14,720
Who are you?

98
00:08:20,220 --> 00:08:21,270
Let's go!

99
00:08:21,270 --> 00:08:22,390
Burglar!

100
00:08:22,390 --> 00:08:23,480
Don't let him get away!

101
00:08:24,230 --> 00:08:25,270
What happened?

102
00:08:25,270 --> 00:08:26,150
What's all this noise?

103
00:08:26,940 --> 00:08:29,230
A burglar trespassed
upon His Highness's room!

104
00:08:29,230 --> 00:08:30,730
I-It can't be!

105
00:08:33,820 --> 00:08:35,200
Oh no...

106
00:08:39,990 --> 00:08:42,250
How merciless this is...

107
00:08:44,750 --> 00:08:49,040
After all he's been through, he never
once saw a father's smile of affection.

108
00:08:52,590 --> 00:08:53,720
Mr. Hassan...

109
00:08:55,930 --> 00:08:57,220
Find the burglar!

110
00:08:57,970 --> 00:09:00,510
You must not let him
get out of the courtyard alive!

111
00:09:00,510 --> 00:09:01,140
Yes, sir!

112
00:09:23,120 --> 00:09:24,370
A sewer...

113
00:09:24,370 --> 00:09:25,210
Find him!

114
00:09:25,210 --> 00:09:26,120
He fell over here!

115
00:09:44,770 --> 00:09:45,730
That sound...

116
00:09:46,810 --> 00:09:48,270
I hear the sound of...

117
00:09:48,850 --> 00:09:49,940
...swords in battle...

118
00:09:55,690 --> 00:09:56,820
Gambino!

119
00:09:59,950 --> 00:10:00,950
That's right...

120
00:10:01,410 --> 00:10:05,080
I always desperately wanted
you to appreciate me.

121
00:10:25,100 --> 00:10:27,270
Stop it!

122
00:11:17,360 --> 00:11:20,780
I bet Griffith is enjoying
a succulent meal right about now.

123
00:11:21,110 --> 00:11:24,910
There are a lot of perks that he can
enjoy at the princess's evening party.

124
00:11:24,910 --> 00:11:27,040
He has nothing to worry about
except for the formalities!

125
00:11:29,120 --> 00:11:31,750
By the way, where is Guts?

126
00:11:32,290 --> 00:11:34,420
I haven't seen him since this morning.

127
00:11:34,420 --> 00:11:38,460
I bet he is busy practicing
with his sword as always!

128
00:11:38,460 --> 00:11:39,920
He is just slacking off!

129
00:11:40,260 --> 00:11:44,890
Our two companies were
supposed to do joint drills today!

130
00:11:44,890 --> 00:11:47,850
Without giving me any notice,
he never showed!

131
00:11:47,850 --> 00:11:49,890
No need to get so furious...

132
00:11:49,890 --> 00:11:51,810
Damn, she's scary!

133
00:11:58,650 --> 00:11:59,570
Guts!

134
00:12:01,150 --> 00:12:03,820
Guts, where have you been
running around all day long?

135
00:12:04,160 --> 00:12:06,280
You caused us a lot
of trouble I'll have you know!

136
00:12:06,780 --> 00:12:09,290
Do you really care about group unity?

137
00:12:11,710 --> 00:12:13,540
Wait, is this an arrow wound?

138
00:12:14,460 --> 00:12:15,710
Griffith...

139
00:12:16,170 --> 00:12:17,500
...where is he?

140
00:12:18,130 --> 00:12:22,380
Griffith is attending Lady Charlotte's
soirée in Promrose Palace.

141
00:12:22,380 --> 00:12:23,260
I see...

142
00:12:24,800 --> 00:12:25,470
Hey!

143
00:12:26,340 --> 00:12:27,600
I'm not finished...

144
00:12:28,930 --> 00:12:30,430
What's wrong with Guts?

145
00:12:50,160 --> 00:12:51,450
Griffith...

146
00:12:57,830 --> 00:12:59,630
I am a little tired...

147
00:13:05,930 --> 00:13:07,800
Please have a seat here.

148
00:13:11,430 --> 00:13:12,430
Thank you.

149
00:13:14,600 --> 00:13:15,310
Wait!

150
00:13:19,310 --> 00:13:21,360
Are you going there
in that shabby outfit?

151
00:13:21,690 --> 00:13:23,530
Don't bring shame to Griffith.

152
00:13:24,190 --> 00:13:27,030
You better wait until they finish
talking if you want to see him!

153
00:13:29,240 --> 00:13:30,280
I'm borrowing this.

154
00:13:41,550 --> 00:13:42,710
H-Hey...

155
00:13:46,840 --> 00:13:52,810
In truth, I am not fond of soirées. They
are clamorous affairs, nothing more.

156
00:13:53,720 --> 00:14:00,060
This one is being held to comfort
those who've fought tirelessly in battles.

157
00:14:00,520 --> 00:14:01,310
But...

158
00:14:01,610 --> 00:14:03,730
I think they should rather...

159
00:14:04,400 --> 00:14:07,780
...stop the war itself than
hold a soirée like this one.

160
00:14:08,610 --> 00:14:12,120
Why do most men commit
themselves to the affair of bloodshed?

161
00:14:12,580 --> 00:14:15,200
You asked me such on
the hunting field, my lady.

162
00:14:15,500 --> 00:14:17,000
Oh, yes...

163
00:14:17,870 --> 00:14:23,130
Indeed, men may have
a barbarous side as you indicate.

164
00:14:23,630 --> 00:14:24,800
However, it is...

165
00:14:25,170 --> 00:14:28,170
...a tool to be used for both claiming
and protecting precious things.

166
00:14:28,470 --> 00:14:30,090
It is a double-edged sword.

167
00:14:30,510 --> 00:14:31,930
Precious things?

168
00:14:31,930 --> 00:14:33,970
Such as family... or lovers?

169
00:14:34,760 --> 00:14:36,600
For some men,
such things are duly cherished.

170
00:14:38,270 --> 00:14:44,070
But there is one other thing more
precious to a man beyond all else...

171
00:14:48,150 --> 00:14:52,820
Something one pursues for one's
own sake and not for that of any other.

172
00:14:52,820 --> 00:14:53,830
A dream.

173
00:14:54,490 --> 00:14:55,540
A dream...

174
00:14:58,330 --> 00:15:00,420
Some dream of ruling the world...

175
00:15:01,370 --> 00:15:04,090
...dedicating their entire life...

176
00:15:04,090 --> 00:15:05,670
...to forging the perfect sword.

177
00:15:06,300 --> 00:15:08,630
While some can be pursued
alone, some are like storms...

178
00:15:09,880 --> 00:15:13,140
...blowing apart hundreds or
thousands of other dreams as they go.

179
00:15:13,760 --> 00:15:16,260
A dream can fortify a man's life,
or it can bring suffering upon it.

180
00:15:16,600 --> 00:15:19,270
A dream can make a man
feel alive, or it can kill him instead.

181
00:15:19,680 --> 00:15:21,980
Even if a man
is abandoned by that dream...

182
00:15:21,980 --> 00:15:24,560
...part of it will remain
smoldering in his heart.

183
00:15:25,980 --> 00:15:29,820
Every man has envisioned
his life in this way, at least once.

184
00:15:30,110 --> 00:15:33,780
A life as a martyr to his dream, his God.

185
00:15:36,160 --> 00:15:39,250
To simply exist just
because one's been born...

186
00:15:39,830 --> 00:15:43,080
...is the sort of notion
that I hate. I can't stand it.

187
00:15:48,300 --> 00:15:51,170
I am sorry. I got carried away.

188
00:15:51,510 --> 00:15:54,090
You must be getting bored.

189
00:15:54,470 --> 00:15:56,100
O-Oh no...

190
00:15:57,720 --> 00:16:02,390
I have never talked
with a man like this before...

191
00:16:03,020 --> 00:16:08,070
I thought you were one of
the aristocracy when I first saw you.

192
00:16:08,610 --> 00:16:11,400
You have so much command
for someone so young.

193
00:16:12,070 --> 00:16:17,080
But on the hunting field, when you
taught me to whistle with a reed...

194
00:16:17,080 --> 00:16:18,120
...you looked...

195
00:16:18,950 --> 00:16:20,660
...like a child.

196
00:16:22,040 --> 00:16:26,750
And now, you are like a philosopher,
enlightening me with your thoughts.

197
00:16:28,710 --> 00:16:30,210
You are marvelous...

198
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:42,310
Your friends must be
fascinated by your charm too.

199
00:16:43,890 --> 00:16:46,190
They are my able soldiers.

200
00:16:46,650 --> 00:16:51,940
They are important comrades who
devote themselves to my dream.

201
00:16:53,070 --> 00:16:55,860
However, they are not necessarily my friends.

202
00:16:57,120 --> 00:17:02,250
In my eyes, a true friend is someone
who never clings to another's dream.

203
00:17:02,790 --> 00:17:05,170
Someone independent...

204
00:17:05,170 --> 00:17:08,670
...who can find his own reason to live
and follow that path without guidance.

205
00:17:09,290 --> 00:17:15,430
And if anyone tries to crush his
dream, protect it heart and soul.

206
00:17:15,880 --> 00:17:19,350
Even if that person happened to be me.

207
00:17:20,510 --> 00:17:22,270
For me, a true friend...

208
00:17:22,770 --> 00:17:25,560
...is someone whom I consider my equal.

209
00:17:38,280 --> 00:17:40,280
You have great confidence in yourself.

210
00:17:42,990 --> 00:17:45,870
That is exactly how I attained everything.

211
00:17:46,710 --> 00:17:47,870
And now...

212
00:17:48,790 --> 00:17:53,250
I am allowed to talk with you,
the princess of the kingdom.

213
00:17:55,130 --> 00:17:57,260
Will you tell me your dream?

214
00:17:58,090 --> 00:17:59,430
Princess!

215
00:18:00,260 --> 00:18:02,060
Something awful has happened!

216
00:18:02,810 --> 00:18:04,020
What ever is the matter?

217
00:18:04,020 --> 00:18:07,310
Your uncle, Count Julius, has been killed!

218
00:18:07,310 --> 00:18:08,480
That cannot be!

219
00:18:08,480 --> 00:18:09,440
He was assassinated!

220
00:18:09,440 --> 00:18:12,980
A burglar broke into his study and
even killed young Master Adonis...

221
00:18:13,820 --> 00:18:15,860
The court has been thrown into an uproar.

222
00:18:35,380 --> 00:18:37,010
What tremendous numbers...

223
00:18:37,010 --> 00:18:41,050
Well, I've heard that the upcoming
battles could end the war.

224
00:18:41,510 --> 00:18:43,560
I hope such a thing becomes reality.

225
00:18:43,560 --> 00:18:44,680
No need to worry!

226
00:18:44,680 --> 00:18:47,520
Midland's army has a guardian angel!

227
00:18:50,440 --> 00:18:51,690
Speak of the devil...

228
00:19:02,200 --> 00:19:04,200
Are you setting out?

229
00:19:07,290 --> 00:19:09,210
Yes, Minister Foss.

230
00:19:09,210 --> 00:19:11,710
We no longer have
General Julius. Only you are left.

231
00:19:12,080 --> 00:19:16,630
You are now the guardian deity of
Midland. I pray for your good fortune...

232
00:19:17,050 --> 00:19:18,300
...in battle.

233
00:19:18,630 --> 00:19:20,840
That seems to be an exaggeration.

234
00:19:21,220 --> 00:19:23,550
However, I shall exert myself to the utmost.

235
00:19:23,550 --> 00:19:29,560
At any rate, I cannot bear
the news of the assassinations.

236
00:19:29,930 --> 00:19:35,060
It is cruel that young Master Adonis
was killed. He was only a child.

237
00:19:35,060 --> 00:19:37,570
Only a devil would do that.

238
00:19:37,570 --> 00:19:39,690
No, it was not a devil's doing.

239
00:19:41,030 --> 00:19:42,860
It was a man's doing, Minister.

240
00:19:45,950 --> 00:19:50,500
By the way, Sir Griffith,
I happened to hear an odd rumor.

241
00:19:50,500 --> 00:19:51,920
An odd rumor?

242
00:19:51,920 --> 00:19:54,960
That the arrow aimed at
Lady Charlotte on the hunting field...

243
00:19:54,960 --> 00:19:58,250
...could possibly have been aimed at you.

244
00:19:58,760 --> 00:20:00,090
Could that be true?

245
00:20:00,090 --> 00:20:02,630
Aiming at a humble unit commander?

246
00:20:02,630 --> 00:20:04,430
According to the rumor...

247
00:20:04,430 --> 00:20:10,230
...the assassin did not hail from
the Tudor Empire, but our own court.

248
00:20:10,770 --> 00:20:12,690
A royal court, you see...

249
00:20:12,690 --> 00:20:15,440
...is like a viper's nest
underneath its graceful facade.

250
00:20:15,440 --> 00:20:20,440
It is no surprise that many people
are brewing up dark plots in the court.

251
00:20:20,440 --> 00:20:21,530
My goodness...

252
00:20:21,530 --> 00:20:23,240
For these people...

253
00:20:23,240 --> 00:20:27,120
It is only a matter of killing a man
inside or outside the castle...

254
00:20:27,120 --> 00:20:29,450
That is the only difference.

255
00:20:29,700 --> 00:20:31,500
That is an interesting theory.

256
00:20:31,960 --> 00:20:33,580
Well, then I will...

257
00:20:33,580 --> 00:20:36,290
...strive to keep any unpleasantries
as far outside the court as possible.

258
00:20:36,670 --> 00:20:37,590
Excuse me.

259
00:20:40,510 --> 00:20:43,130
He did not even bat an eyelash!

260
00:20:43,130 --> 00:20:45,550
Does that mean it was not his doing?

261
00:20:47,850 --> 00:20:49,510
No, that cannot be.

262
00:20:49,510 --> 00:20:51,930
If it were an accident,
it would be far too good to be true.

263
00:20:54,190 --> 00:20:57,060
W-Wait, could it be that
he knows about me?

264
00:20:58,730 --> 00:21:01,900
No, no man could discover my
intrigue, however keen he is.

265
00:21:01,900 --> 00:21:04,200
Besides, there is no evidence left.

266
00:21:28,590 --> 00:21:30,850
For me, a true friend...

267
00:21:30,850 --> 00:21:33,560
...is someone whom I consider my equal.

268
00:22:03,390 --> 00:22:05,850
Looking back, the morning comes.

269
00:22:05,850 --> 00:22:09,350
Don't find your face in your glass.

270
00:22:10,390 --> 00:22:13,480
Take the moonlight by the tail.

271
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:16,440
It's a rainy sight. You're shading.

272
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:19,650
What is that?

273
00:22:19,650 --> 00:22:20,900
It's just the same.

274
00:22:20,900 --> 00:22:24,070
What is trying your crown?

275
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:28,370
I'm spending my glass, walking back.

276
00:22:28,370 --> 00:22:31,410
So wear my glass. You're fading.

277
00:22:31,710 --> 00:22:51,310
I'm waiting so long.

278
00:22:51,310 --> 00:23:00,400
I'm waiting...

